KG42.register("rules-5bd4d3c5de00ed604f868796",{"id":"05-double_auction::v141-c-R007","paper":"05-double_auction","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R007","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Consumer participation","process_stage":"participation","market_meaning":"Buyers must not incur negative utilities from participating in discriminatory k-DA. Scope: Buyer participation in discriminatory k-DA.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function participation.consumer under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["participation.consumer"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Buyer participation in discriminatory k-DA.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-09"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Buyers must not incur negative utilities from participating in discriminatory k-DA. Scope: Buyer participation in discriminatory k-DA.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-09"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-09","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p03-c1r3__v141-a-M01-validation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1","anchor_text":"g p all individual utilities for social welfare such that no participants are precluded from trading","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"An ideal auction mechanism encompasses four distinct properties: individual rationality (IR), budget balance (BB), incentive compatibility (IC), and economic efficiency (EE) [47]. An IR mechanism implies that no buyers/sellers shall result in negative utilities from participating in the auction. All four reviewed mechanisms exhibit IR. A BB mechanism does not financially subsidize or gain from transactions between buyers and sellers. Both VCG and TR are not BB as their market operators financially subsidize and gain from trades, respectively. IC motivates participants to bid their valuations truthfully. Both Discriminatory and Uniform k-DA do not have mechanisms to motivate truthful bidding as VCG and TR do. EE attempts to maximize the sum of all individual utilities for social welfare such that no participants are precluded from trading. Since buyer $\\gamma$ and seller $\\gamma$ are precluded from trading in TR, the mechanism, by default, does not maximize economic efficiency. While an ideal auction mechanism shall exhibit all four properties, it is important to note that the Myerson-Satterthwaite theorem [48] proves that no realistic mechanism can exhibit these four properties simultaneously."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"No variable can be declared because the source's IR statement for participation is verbal and the utility symbol defined in the source (U_i^{strategy}) belongs to the bidding stage; formalizing it would require nodes (bidding.demand, pricing.local) and edges absent from this rule's frozen graph and unreviewed B evidence.","empty_theta_reason":"No parameter is declared in the source for the IR participation condition; the symbols B^P, S^P and p are variables of other stages, not fixed constants, and their nodes/edges are outside this rule's frozen graph."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-validation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"participation.consumer","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-09","quote":"An IR mechanism implies that no buyers/sellers shall result in negative utilities from participating in the auction. All four reviewed mechanisms exhibit IR."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"fdedb7b38b20886d5cf6f2d0985a3bbcde7b389839eb9d8a82d14690895b77a2","applicability":"needs_revision","reason":"The frozen graph has V=['participation.consumer'] and E=[], with no x/theta. The only attached evidence v141-b-g01-ev-09 states individual rationality verbally: 'no buyers/sellers shall result in negative utilities from participating in the auction.' A faithful formalization would require a buyer-utility variable and the individual-rationality trading condition p ≤ B^P (same-mechanism candidate evidence v141-b-g02-E23), which references nodes pricing.local and bidding.demand absent from this rule's V/E. Because the graph cannot represent the source formula without adding nodes/edges, and the B evidence remains unreviewed, the rule is needs_revision. C001 is preserved as not_formalized.","bindings":[],"revision_requests":["Request C.1 to add nodes bidding.demand and pricing.local (or a dedicated buyer-utility node) and edges linking participation.consumer to the IR trade condition so that the source formula p ≤ B^P (buyer) can be bound and formalized.","Request B to extract or confirm the exact mathematical definition of the utility used for the IR property (e.g., B^P − p or ξ_i − χ_i^{strategy}) and its domain/unit; currently only the verbal statement 'no negative utilities' is available (v141-b-g01-ev-09, source_status unverified).","Confirm whether this rule is intended as a procedural admission rule (non_mathematical) or a mathematical IR condition; if mathematical, supply the graph elements needed for formalization. Candidate same-mechanism evidence v141-b-g02-E23 and v141-b-g01-ev-15 exist but remain unreviewed and unaudited."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
